    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d601-a1">

                <pb facs="1055" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg955"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    247.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Swiss Federal Council to Mr. Fish</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-01-12"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 12,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>A certain George Retschel or Ritschel, a native of the Grand Duchy of Baden, hut
                    naturalized as an American citizen at Philadelphia the 22d of April, 1856, as
                    appears from the document herewith inclosed, has fallen ill at Boujean near
                    Bienne, canton of Berne, and his wife is not in a position to provide
                    subsistence for the family, consequently the government; of the canton of Berne
                    requests that the chargé d’affaires of the United States should furnish
                    assistance sufficient to enable this unfortunate family to subsist.</p>
                <p>In transmitting this request to Mr. Fish, and in asking him kindly to return the
                    certificate of Retschel’s naturalization, the Federal Council seizes this
                    occasion, &amp;c.,</p>
                <p>In the name of the Federal Council.</p>
                <closer>The President of the Confederation:<lb/><signed>WELTI.</signed><lb/>The
                    chancellor of the Confederation:<lb/><signed>SCHIESS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
